---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import { products } from "@/data/products";

const withPolicy = products.filter((p) => p.policy);
---

<Base title="Website Privacy — What Spolvero Collects, and Why It Does" description="What spolvero.design collects when you visit and why: analytics, forms and advertising, plus how each one is limited and what you can turn off.">
  <section class="bg-primary py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container-page">
      <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-col items-center text-center">
        <span class="text-md font-semibold text-brand-secondary">Updated 17 September 2026</span>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-display-md font-semibold text-primary md:text-display-lg">Website privacy</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-tertiary md:text-xl">This covers spolvero.design only. Each app has its own privacy policy.</p>
      </div>
      <article class="prose mx-auto mt-12 max-w-3xl md:prose-lg md:mt-16">
        <h2>Visitor statistics</h2>
        <p>
          We use Google Analytics to count visits and see which pages are read, so we know what to improve. It records things
          like the pages you view, how you arrived, your approximate location, and your device and browser type. We don't use it
          for advertising, and advertising cookies are turned off.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you visit from the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, Google Analytics does not set
          cookies. Google receives only basic, cookie-less signals. How Google handles this data is described at
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.
          You can also block it with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>How the site is used</h2>
        <p>
          We also use Microsoft Clarity to understand how people use the site. Clarity records clicks, scrolling and mouse
          movement, and can replay a visit as a session recording, so we can find confusing parts of a page. Anything you type
          into a form is masked and not recorded. Advertising use is turned off, and if your device is set to a European
          timezone, Clarity does not set cookies. See
          <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement">Microsoft's privacy statement</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Forms</h2>
        <p>
          When you use the contact form or join the launch list, what you type (and any file you attach) is sent to us by
          email through FormSubmit, a form-delivery service. We use it only to reply to you or to tell you about launches, and
          we don't sell it or share it with anyone else. To be removed from the launch list, or to have a message deleted,
          email <a href="mailto:spolvero.design@gmail.com">spolvero.design@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, which records visitors' IP addresses in its logs for security. See
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Our apps</h2>
        <p>Each app handles your data differently. Read its own policy:</p>
        <ul>
          {withPolicy.map((p) => <li><a href={`/${p.slug}/privacy/`}>{p.storeName}</a></li>)}
        </ul>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p><a href="mailto:spolvero.design@gmail.com">spolvero.design@gmail.com</a></p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
